            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Kodiak AI debuts via SPAC deal. CEO discusses its driverless trucks.",
            "description": "<p>Kodiak AI (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/KDK\">KDK</a>) began publicly trading on the Nasdaq via a SPAC deal (Special Purpose Acquisition Company) on Thursday. Autonomous trucking startup Kodiak Robotics merged with Ares Acquisition Corp. II (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AACT\">AACT</a>) to form the new company.</p>\n<p>Kodiak AI founder and CEO Don Burnette joins Market Catalysts host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/julie-hyman/?.tsrc=fin-srch\">Julie Hyman</a> for a conversation about the company's driverless trucking technology and customer base.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
